Alternative, minimal fix for touchscreen taps being lost under LCL-gtk3.

Stop putting GDK_TOUCH_MASK in GDK_DEFAULT_EVENTS_MASK, so LCL widgets no
longer ask for touch events and X/GDK go back to emulating the mouse for the
first finger. Smaller than 0001, but it relies on nothing else in the window
selecting touch events: if a GTK parent (e.g. a client-side-decorated
GtkWindow with gestures) selects them, pointer emulation can still be
suppressed. See ../ANALYSIS.md.

Against Lazarus main b9cfd22ae9 (2026-09-11). Applies cleanly and compiles
with FPC 3.3.1 with no errors (gtk3procs.pas, and gtk3widgets.pas built
against it). Not tested on touch hardware.

--- a/lcl/interfaces/gtk3/gtk3procs.pas	2026-09-11 19:15:50.797367025 -0400
+++ b/lcl/interfaces/gtk3/gtk3procs.pas	2026-09-11 19:15:50.799492670 -0400
@@ -117,8 +117,10 @@
     GDK_PROXIMITY_IN_MASK, {262144}
     GDK_PROXIMITY_OUT_MASK, {524288}
     GDK_SUBSTRUCTURE_MASK, {1048576}
-    GDK_SCROLL_MASK, {2097152}
-    GDK_TOUCH_MASK {4194304}
+    GDK_SCROLL_MASK {2097152}
+    // GDK_TOUCH_MASK {4194304} - not selected: asking for touch events stops
+    // X/GDK emulating the mouse for touches, and LCL does not handle
+    // GDK_TOUCH_*, so every tap on a touchscreen was lost.
  // GDK_SMOOTH_SCROLL_MASK {8388608} //there is a bug in GTK3, see https://stackoverflow.com/questions/11775161/gtk3-get-mouse-scroll-direction
   ];
 
